#: src/app/[locale]/[...slug]/music.tsx:83
msgid ""
"Ruckgaber also composed songs for a voice with the piano with\n"
"              Polish lyrics. After the November uprising of 1830, he composed\n"
"              the song &quot;Do mogił&quot; (Towards the Graves) to the words by\n"
"              Wincenty Pol."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/[...slug]/music.tsx:37
msgid ""
"Ruckgaber contributed to the evolution of the musical profession\n"
"              from being an inspired composer, dependent on a patron, to a\n"
"              self-reliant, conscious artist, who influenced public taste and\n"
"              demand of the culture market."
msgstr ""
"Ruckgaber contribuyó a la evolución de la profesión musical\n"
"              de ser un compositor inspirado, dependiente de un mecenas, a un\n"
"              artista autónomo y consciente, que influyó en el gusto público y\n"
"              la demanda del mercado cultural."

#: src/app/[locale]/[...slug]/music.tsx:30
msgid ""
"Ruckgaber’s work and music fully belong to the current of early\n"
"              Romanticism. His compositions reflected the leading aesthetic\n"
"              trends of the era. Early Romanticism showed in seeking lyrical\n"
"              modes of expression, in transforming the canons of classicism, and\n"
"              in the development of the so-called salon music."
msgstr "La obra y la música de Ruckgaber pertenecen completamente a la corriente del primer Romanticismo. Sus composiciones reflejaban las principales tendencias estéticas de la época. El primer Romanticismo se manifestaba en la búsqueda de modos de expresión líricos, en la transformación de los cánones del clasicismo y en el desarrollo de la llamada música de salón."

